Appendix II – Metadata on SGIF Information

The SGIF SQL database contains systematically organized rural fire data since 2001. It also includes data on other topics related to rural fires, such as meteorology, orography, infrastructure, and land use. The following table presents the list and description of the variables associated with each rural fire.


VARIABLE	DESCRIPTION
Codigo	SGIF code of the fire (Forest Service); unique key linking all PRFD files
CodigoSado	SADO code of the fire (Civil Protection)
Ano	Year of the alert date
Dia	Day of the alert date
Mes	Month of the alert date
Hora	Hour of the alert
Tipo	Fire type (forest or agricultural)
DHInicio	Date/time of the alert (start of the fire; never imputed)
DH1Intervencao	Date/time of the first intervention
DHResolucao	Date/time of the resolution
DHConclusao	Date/time of the conclusion
DHFim	Date/time of extinction (departure of the last firefighting team), as reported
DHFimEstimado	Date/time of extinction after the correction rules and multiple imputation (median of 10 imputations); see DHFim_Rules and Observacoes
DuracaoHoras	Fire duration, as reported
DuracaoHorasEstimado	Fire duration after the correction rules and multiple imputation (median of 10 imputations)
Tempo1Intervencao	Time between the alert and the first intervention
TempoResolucao	Time between the first intervention and the resolution
TempoRescaldo	Time between the resolution and the conclusion (mop-up)
NUTS2	NUTS II region of the point of origin
NUTS3	NUTS III region of the point of origin
Distrito	District of the point of origin (harmonized)
Concelho	Municipality of the point of origin (harmonized)
Freguesia	Parish of the point of origin (harmonized)
Freguesia2014	[VERIFY] Parish of the point of origin after the 2013 administrative reorganization
Local	Toponym (nearest place name) of the point of origin
INE	INE code of the parish of the point of origin
DDCCFF2014	[VERIFY] DICOFRE code (district-municipality-parish) of the parish, 2013 reorganization
QO	Operational grid cell (1 x 1 km) of the point of origin
x_20790	X coordinate, EPSG:20790 (Lisbon / Portuguese National Grid)
y_20790	Y coordinate, EPSG:20790 (Lisbon / Portuguese National Grid)
x_3763	X coordinate, EPSG:3763 (ETRS89 / PT-TM06)
y_3763	Y coordinate, EPSG:3763 (ETRS89 / PT-TM06)
Lat_4326	Latitude, EPSG:4326 (WGS 84)
Lon_4326	Longitude, EPSG:4326 (WGS 84)
AreaPov	Burned area of forest stands, as reported
AreaMato	Burned area of shrublands, as reported
AreaAgric	Burned area of agricultural land, as reported
AreaTotal	Total burned area, as reported
AreaTotalEstimada	Total burned area after multiple imputation of zero or missing values (median of 10 imputations); equal to AreaTotal when observed
HaHora	Burned area per hour (AreaTotal / DuracaoHoras), as reported
HaHoraEstimado	Burned area per hour from the estimated area and duration
ClasseArea	Burned-area class
CodCausa	Cause code, harmonized across periods t1-t5 to the current SGIF list
TipoCausa	Type of cause
GrupoCausa	Cause group
DescricaoCausa	Description of the cause
Reacendimento	Reignition flag (1 if the fire is a reignition)
Reacendimento_IncendioPai	If a reignition, code of the parent fire
OriginouReacendimento	Fire caused a reignition (0 or 1)
Reacendimentos	[VERIFY] Number of reignitions originated by the fire
FonteAlerta	Source of the alert
AltitudeMedia	Mean altitude of the 1 x 1 km cell of the point of origin (25 m DEM)
DecliveMedio	Mean slope of the 1 x 1 km cell of the point of origin
HorasExposicaoMedia	Mean annual solar exposure at the point of origin
Rugosidade	Terrain ruggedness index (Riley et al., 1999)
Perimetro	National forest or forest perimeter at the point of origin
APS	Protected area (RNAP) at the point of origin
ModFarsite	Fuel model at the point of origin (Fernandes and Loureiro, 2021)
AreaManchaModFarsite	Area of the fuel-model patch at the point of origin
RCM	IPMA rural fire risk index (RCM)
DendidadeRV	Road density in the 1 x 1 km cell of the point of origin
CosN5Variedade	Number of distinct COS level-5 land-use classes in the 1 x 1 km cell
Perigosidade	Structural fire hazard level (Verde and Zezere, 2010)
Dist_CBS_m	Straight-line distance to the nearest fire station
CBS	Nearest fire station (straight line)
DensidadeResidentes	Resident population density of the nearest statistical subsection
DensidadeEdificios	Building density of the nearest statistical subsection
AreaTotalIncSimul5000	Sum of the burned areas of fires simultaneously active with the recorded fire and with origin within 5 km
NIncSimulDistrito	Number of fires simultaneously active (fully or partially) with the recorded fire, with origin in the same district
NIncSimulConcelho	Number of fires simultaneously active (fully or partially) with the recorded fire, with origin in the same municipality
NIncSimulDistrito90	Number of fires active during the first 90 min after the alert of the recorded fire, with origin in the same district
NIncSimulConcelho90	Number of fires active during the first 90 min after the alert of the recorded fire, with origin in the same municipality
NIncSimul500090	Number of fires active during the first 90 min after the alert of the recorded fire, with origin within 5 km
DistIncSimul500090	[VERIFY] Number of fires active during the first 90 min after the alert, with origin in the same district and within 5 km
AreaTotalIncSimul500090	Sum of the burned areas of fires active during the first 90 min after the alert, with origin in the same district and within 5 km
EstadoRegisto	[VERIFY] Status of the record in SGIF
Temperatura	Air temperature at 2 m at the hour of the alert
HumidadeRelativa	Relative humidity at the hour of the alert
VentoIntensidade	Wind speed at 10 m at the hour of the alert
VentoIntensidade_vetor	Wind speed of the resultant wind vector
VentoDirecao_vetor	Wind direction of the resultant wind vector
Precepitacao	Precipitation
VentoDirecao	Wind direction at the hour of the alert
fwi	Daily Fire Weather Index at the point of origin, alert date
dsr	Daily Severity Rating
isi	Daily Initial Spread Index
dc	Daily Drought Code
dmc	Daily Duff Moisture Code
ffmc	Daily Fine Fuel Moisture Code
bui	Daily Buildup Index
hFWI	Hourly FWI at the hour of the alert
hFFMC	Hourly FFMC at the hour of the alert
hISI	Hourly ISI at the hour of the alert
MaxFWIh_48h_PosExtincao	Maximum hourly FWI in the 48 h after extinction
MaxFFMCh_48h_PosExtincao	Maximum hourly FFMC in the 48 h after extinction
MaxISIh_48h_PosExtincao	Maximum hourly ISI in the 48 h after extinction
MaxDC_48h_DiaPosExtincao	Maximum daily DC in the 48 h after extinction
MaxDMC_48h_PosExtincao	Maximum DMC in the 48 h after extinction
MaxBUI_48h_PosExtincao	Maximum BUI in the 48 h after extinction
NIncSimul5000	Number of fires simultaneously active (fully or partially) with the recorded fire, with origin within 5 km
DistIncSimul5000	[VERIFY] Number of fires simultaneously active with the recorded fire, with origin in the same district and within 5 km
ClassificacaoRegisto	[VERIFY] Classification of the record in SGIF
Observacoes	Notes; marked 'estimated' or 'anomaly' when timestamps or area were corrected or imputed
NIncSimul5000_Estimado	As NIncSimul5000, computed with the estimated end times
NIncSimulConcelho_Estimado	As NIncSimulConcelho, computed with the estimated end times
NIncSimulDistrito_Estimado	As NIncSimulDistrito, computed with the estimated end times
NIncSimul500090_Estimado	As NIncSimul500090, computed with the estimated end times
NIncSimulConcelho90_Estimado	As NIncSimulConcelho90, computed with the estimated end times
NIncSimulDistrito90_Estimado	As NIncSimulDistrito90, computed with the estimated end times
BACodAssociacao	Code of the fire used to attach the PBA perimeter (equal to Codigo for every record). Not a link indicator: linked records have a non-empty geom or a value in BAMetodo
BACodEstimado	Code of the fire proposed by the matching algorithm for the linked PBA perimeter (may differ from Codigo when the link was made manually)
BAMetodo	Method of the PBA link: BLIND, PAFA or FRP; empty when no perimeter is linked
BAScore	Similarity score S_ij of the PBA link (Eq. 1); lower is better; > 0.6 = low confidence
BAMetodoManual	'Manual Introduction' when the PBA perimeter carries the fire code entered manually by ICNF; empty otherwise
IDPT.FireSprd	Fire ID in PT-FireSprd (Benali et al., 2023), for the 84 cross-referenced major fires (column IDPT-FireSprd in the GeoPackage)
Effis_Muito_Baixa_perc	Share of the linked perimeter in the EFFIS Very Low severity class (Sentinel-2, 2018-2025)
Effis_Baixa_perc	Share of the linked perimeter in the EFFIS Low severity class
Effis_MÃ©dia_perc	Share of the linked perimeter in the EFFIS Moderate severity class
Effis_Alta_perc	Share of the linked perimeter in the EFFIS High severity class
Effis_Muito_Alta_perc	Share of the linked perimeter in the EFFIS Very High severity class
PBSA_Muito_Baixa_perc	Share of the linked perimeter with dNBR < 0.10 (Landsat, fires >= 100 ha, 1984-2022)
PBSA_Baixa_perc	Share of the linked perimeter with dNBR 0.10-0.27
PBSA_MÃ©dia_perc	Share of the linked perimeter with dNBR 0.27-0.44
PBSA_Alta_perc	Share of the linked perimeter with dNBR 0.44-0.66
PBSA_Muito_Alta_perc	Share of the linked perimeter with dNBR >= 0.66
gpp_8d	Gross primary productivity of the last 8-day composite before ignition (500 m; 2001-2025)
gpp_acum_ms	[VERIFY] GPP accumulated since 1 January, converted to dry matter (NPP/GPP = 0.5; 2.2 g DM per g C)
fapar	Fraction of absorbed PAR, last composite before ignition (main algorithm only)
lai	Leaf area index, last composite before ignition (main algorithm only)
ndvi	NDVI, last 16-day composite before ignition (good or marginal reliability)
evi	EVI, last 16-day composite before ignition (good or marginal reliability)
ndii7	NDII7 = (NIR - SWIR 2.1 um) / (NIR + SWIR 2.1 um), last 16-day composite before ignition
Funcao	Phase in which FRE was computed: Poligono (fire with a PBA perimeter), Ponto (fire without perimeter, >= 0.5 ha of reported burned area, from the ignition point), or Nenhum (no hotspot assigned)
FRE	Sum of the FRP of the hotspots assigned to the fire, one value per 15-min SEVIRI slot (FRE_GJ = 0.9 x FRE)
Num_Pontos_FRP	Number of SEVIRI FRP hotspots assigned to the fire
FRE_GJ	Fire Radiative Energy, time-integrated SEVIRI FRP (2004-2024; fires with a linked perimeter)
geom	Burned-area perimeter (PBA) linked to the fire (polygon, EPSG:3763); empty when the fire has no linked perimeter. Geometry of the layer fogos in PRFD.gpkg; not in the CSV. The ignition point is given by x_3763 / y_3763 (or the other coordinate fields)


